&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 8pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. RELATED PARTY TRANSACTIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Operations and Maintenance Agreement.&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;On June 26, 2019, Double E and Summit Permian II entered into an Operations and Maintenance Agreement, as amended ("OMA") relating to the operation of the Project. Summit Permian II operates the pipeline in accordance with the terms of the OMA. The OMA may be terminated upon mutual written consent, upon the resignation of Summit Permian II or upon the removal of Summit Permian II in accordance with the provisions of the OMA.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;Upon commissioning the pipeline in November 2021, Summit Permian II began receiving compensation under the OMA of approximately $0.3 million per month. During each of the six months ended June 30, 2026 and 2025, Double E incurred $1.8 million of costs from Summit Permian II under the terms of the OMA, which is recorded within Operations Expense in the statement of income.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 8pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
